course: dictionary
lesson: 6221
title: Misuse: using things the wrong way
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Misuse means using something in a wrong, careless or harmful way. Look at the start of the word: mis- means wrong or badly, as in misread or misspell. «Substance misuse» is the official phrase for harmful use of drugs or alcohol. The clue is misuse, and the word harmful tells you it is bad.
explain: Misuse can be a noun or a verb, and the sound changes. As a noun, say mis-YOOS: «misuse of medicine» or «misuse of power». As a verb, say mis-YOOZ: «Do not misuse the fire alarm.» Read the words around it to decide which one it is.
explain: Misuse is not only about things. «Anonymous reporting means telling without giving your name.» It can protect the reporter, but it can also be misused to spread false stories. So when you see misuse, ask: what was used, and was it used wrongly?
fact: Misuse means using something in a wrong, careless or harmful way.
fact: As a noun, misuse is said mis-YOOS, as in «misuse of medicine». As a verb, it is said mis-YOOZ.
fact: In safety lessons, misusing medicines, fire alarms or emergency numbers is dangerous and sometimes against the law.
fact: Getting into a computer or account without permission is illegal in most countries; in the UK, it is against the Computer Misuse Act 1990.
fact: Anonymous reporting can be misused to spread false stories, so always think before you believe or share.
exercise: «Substance misuse» is the official phrase for what? | Helpful use of school books | *Harmful use of drugs or alcohol | Sharing food with friends at lunch
exercise: Ella says misuse means using something properly and carefully. Is she right? | Yes, misuse means using something properly | *No, misuse means using something in a wrong, careless or harmful way | Yes, but only with a computer
exercise: Which of these is an example of misuse of a fire alarm? | Checking with your teacher that it works | *Pressing it as a joke when there is no fire | Learning where it is in the building | Reading the safety sign next to it
test: «Anonymous reporting can be misused to spread false stories.» What can be misused in this sentence? | *Anonymous reporting | Your handwriting | The sun | The school library
test: Which word means the wrong or harmful use of something? | Museum | *Misuse | Mouse | Music
exam: In the UK, which law makes getting into a computer without permission illegal? | *The Computer Misuse Act 1990 | The Computer Games Act 1990 | The Computer Lessons Act 1990 | The Computer Sharing Act 1990
